(5852772, 850864, 83313, '<td valign="top">I like this, except for the tight cropping on the left of the building. I suspect that there may have been something to the left that would have hurt the scene more than the tight crop.</td>', 'I like this, except for the tight cropping on the left of the building. I suspect that there may have been something to the left that would have hurt the scene more than the tight crop.', '2010-02-04 12:56:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852781, 850958, 83313, '<td valign="top">Seems overall slightly out of focus and not quite grabbing me visually. Might be a really good shot to do as a grainy, moody b/w.</td>', 'Seems overall slightly out of focus and not quite grabbing me visually. Might be a really good shot to do as a grainy, moody b/w.', '2010-02-04 13:01:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852798, 851187, 83313, '<td valign="top">A fork in the road? Reminds me of <a href="//www.youtube.com/watch?v=WVn6Yz9W-ng" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this</a>.</td>', 'A fork in the road? Reminds me of this.', '2010-02-04 13:08:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852805, 850986, 83313, '<td valign="top">It does look like a human figure marching onward. An interesting abstract play of light and shadow.</td>', 'It does look like a human figure marching onward. An interesting abstract play of light and shadow.', '2010-02-04 13:10:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852831, 850569, 83313, '<td valign="top">I''m sure you are already getting beat up on this pretty badly, but I still feel obliged to give the courtesy an explanation for my own low vote, so here goes:<br/> <br/>-Harsh onboard flash is not flattering to the subject. It rarely is. <br/>-Top of her head is lopped off by the frame<br/>-Very grainy, high ISO shot.<br/> <br/>Such indoor low light conditions are usually tough to work with.  Using a tripod, lower ISO and lower shutter speed could possibly allow you to get a more pleasing shot with the ambient light. If you have a camera with a hotshoe, getting an external flash that you can rotate to bounce off the ceiling is also a good option.<br/> <br/>Sorry to have to be so hard on this entry.</td>', 'I''m sure you are already getting beat up on this pretty badly, but I still feel obliged to give the courtesy an explanation for my own low vote, so here goes: -Harsh onboard flash is not flattering to the subject. It rarely is. -Top of her head is lopped off by the frame-Very grainy, high ISO shot. Such indoor low light conditions are usually tough to work with.  Using a tripod, lower ISO and lower shutter speed could possibly allow you to get a more pleasing shot with the ambient light. If you have a camera with a hotshoe, getting an external flash that you can rotate to bounce off the ceiling is also a good option. Sorry to have to be so hard on this entry.', '2010-02-04 13:21:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852834, 851200, 83313, '<td valign="top">Neat looking abstract imagery.</td>', 'Neat looking abstract imagery.', '2010-02-04 13:22:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852839, 851276, 83313, '<td valign="top">This strikes me as a spur of the moment portrait. Love it! she''s very pretty and the soft light is wonderful. My only nitpick is the bright light at the end of the walkway tends to draw my eye a bit. Still gets a high vote from me. In spite of that nitpick I find this to be a captivating portrait of a very pretty woman.</td>', 'This strikes me as a spur of the moment portrait. Love it! she''s very pretty and the soft light is wonderful. My only nitpick is the bright light at the end of the walkway tends to draw my eye a bit. Still gets a high vote from me. In spite of that nitpick I find this to be a captivating portrait of a very pretty woman.', '2010-02-04 13:26:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852844, 850010, 83313, '<td valign="top">There is a lack of clarity to this photo and I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 58k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a lot of the detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit. <br/> <br/>I will probably be the only one anal enough about compression to notice that.</td>', 'There is a lack of clarity to this photo and I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 58k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a lot of the detail and sharpness from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit.  I will probably be the only one anal enough about compression to notice that.', '2010-02-04 13:28:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852851, 846798, 83313, '<td valign="top">There is a lack of sharpness and detail to this photo and I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 10k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a most of the clarity from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit.</td>', 'There is a lack of sharpness and detail to this photo and I think most of it is due to the use of excessive JPEG compression. Your file size of only 10k indicates a highly compressed image and that is what is robbing a most of the clarity from this image. Check your compression settings when you save your file. Always adjust JPEG compression so that your file size is as large as possible, but within the challenge limit.', '2010-02-04 13:29:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5852857, 849907, 83313, '<td valign="top">The harsh onboard flash is a problem, but I think under these circumstances, you didn''t have anything else you could do. You captured this well for the conditions you were clearly shooting in.</td>', 'The harsh onboard flash is a problem, but I think under these circumstances, you didn''t have anything else you could do. You captured this well for the conditions you were clearly shooting in.', '2010-02-04 13:32:31.000000', NULL, 1),
