(5856870, 850404, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: My, what a compellingly subtle portrait - there is something about the slight ''miss'' of focus that grabs you in a way a super-sharp image could not. I love the coloration too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Beyond a simple ''capture-the-face'' portrait. Excellent.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: My, what a compellingly subtle portrait - there is something about the slight ''miss'' of focus that grabs you in a way a super-sharp image could not. I love the coloration too. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Beyond a simple ''capture-the-face'' portrait. Excellent.', '2010-02-07 14:18:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856871, 849962, 96881, '<td valign="top">Dont know why you put (no edit) in the title.........it makes no difference to me whether you edited it or not.  However, highlighting that, for whatever reason, also makes me think why you didnt bother to edit the photo, and highlights to me what I would have done in editing.  let the image, edited or not, speak for itself...........</td>', 'Dont know why you put (no edit) in the title.........it makes no difference to me whether you edited it or not.  However, highlighting that, for whatever reason, also makes me think why you didnt bother to edit the photo, and highlights to me what I would have done in editing.  let the image, edited or not, speak for itself...........', '2010-02-07 14:18:33.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856872, 849417, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Startling POV and interesting subjects - the fixed stare is excellent, love the canvas ''overlay''.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much really, there is obviously plenty of negative space - I like that, others may not.. but I don''t think that will bother you too much! :-)<br/> <br/>Overall: A very effective composition with compelling subjects.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Startling POV and interesting subjects - the fixed stare is excellent, love the canvas ''overlay''. Critical stuff: Not much really, there is obviously plenty of negative space - I like that, others may not.. but I don''t think that will bother you too much! :-) Overall: A very effective composition with compelling subjects.', '2010-02-07 14:19:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856873, 850955, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Pigeons on vacation! I like it! Tons of dynamism here, the image feels like it exploding - I particularly like the shadows.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Perhaps the surf line is throwing my eye out but the horizon looks slight off to me - a tad lower on the left.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great capture - you''ve made me feel like I was got to see this happen for real. Great job.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Pigeons on vacation! I like it! Tons of dynamism here, the image feels like it exploding - I particularly like the shadows. Critical stuff: Perhaps the surf line is throwing my eye out but the horizon looks slight off to me - a tad lower on the left. Overall: A great capture - you''ve made me feel like I was got to see this happen for real. Great job.', '2010-02-07 14:19:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856875, 851187, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Ordinary object, unusual context - found or placed? I remember someone did a 30 days of forks; I wonder if this is part of a similar project. <br/> <br/>Critical stuff: The depth of field is pretty narrow here, I would have thought that a wider DOF that took in the whole fork might have been more effective - something with a very small sensor like a phone camera would have fitted the bill.<br/> <br/>Overall: A difficult one for me this, I quite like the overall image but I can''t say I find it very interesting and I can''t quite understand your rationale for offering it up for the FS. I wish I could.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Ordinary object, unusual context - found or placed? I remember someone did a 30 days of forks; I wonder if this is part of a similar project.  Critical stuff: The depth of field is pretty narrow here, I would have thought that a wider DOF that took in the whole fork might have been more effective - something with a very small sensor like a phone camera would have fitted the bill. Overall: A difficult one for me this, I quite like the overall image but I can''t say I find it very interesting and I can''t quite understand your rationale for offering it up for the FS. I wish I could.', '2010-02-07 14:19:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856901, 851153, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is beautiful - quite Turner-esque.</td>', 'This is beautiful - quite Turner-esque.', '2010-02-07 14:50:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856902, 851198, 100393, '<td valign="top">Sensational portrait work (as ever!)</td>', 'Sensational portrait work (as ever!)', '2010-02-07 14:51:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856906, 849414, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I really like this - the silhouette (and partials) are just right, the background nice and sparkly and I like that we can tell they have a purposeful stride.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: You know I''m going to mention the rail at the bottom right of the image... just one step to the left! Also, the figures appear slightly halo-ish - is this the consequence of an aggressive edit?<br/> <br/>Overall: An effective image but given the handrail, I might have been tempted to crop just behind the leading woman</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I really like this - the silhouette (and partials) are just right, the background nice and sparkly and I like that we can tell they have a purposeful stride. Critical stuff: You know I''m going to mention the rail at the bottom right of the image... just one step to the left! Also, the figures appear slightly halo-ish - is this the consequence of an aggressive edit? Overall: An effective image but given the handrail, I might have been tempted to crop just behind the leading woman', '2010-02-07 14:55:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856907, 846683, 61961, '<td valign="top">Very pretty, I love the bits of white and red and of course the light through the bird''s wings is fantastic.  Good comp, though there''s a rounded blue something on the right that keeps drawing my eye.</td>', 'Very pretty, I love the bits of white and red and of course the light through the bird''s wings is fantastic.  Good comp, though there''s a rounded blue something on the right that keeps drawing my eye.', '2010-02-07 14:56:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856909, 850730, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Excellent, excellent, excellent!! This is just brilliant. Bags of story, nicely executed and highly original.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing at all.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very, very good.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Excellent, excellent, excellent!! This is just brilliant. Bags of story, nicely executed and highly original. Critical stuff: Nothing at all. Overall: Very, very good.', '2010-02-07 14:56:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856911, 846145, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Definitely unconventional! I really like the idea behind this shot and the props are well suited.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think something this quirky would be better matched with less vanilla POV and editing - I''m not sure this front on, edited with the flat light look suits the image.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice but I don''t think you''ve got the maximum amount of interest out of this intriguing scene.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Definitely unconventional! I really like the idea behind this shot and the props are well suited. Critical stuff: I think something this quirky would be better matched with less vanilla POV and editing - I''m not sure this front on, edited with the flat light look suits the image. Overall: Nice but I don''t think you''ve got the maximum amount of interest out of this intriguing scene.', '2010-02-07 15:00:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856912, 851282, 61961, '<td valign="top">A familiar building, one I''ve photographed myself.  Perhaps this is <img alt="'' . substr(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif"/> <a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=100831" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">PennyStreet</a>?  Very colorful!</td>', 'A familiar building, one I''ve photographed myself.  Perhaps this is  PennyStreet?  Very colorful!', '2010-02-07 15:00:50.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856915, 847630, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very nice indeed.</td>', 'Very nice indeed.', '2010-02-07 15:01:27.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856920, 849962, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Straight out of the camera eh? Nicely done. Very interesting combination of subjects - I like how there is a linking theme of ''lines''. I find the orange luminance highly intriguing.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much really, hard to argue with a zero edit - suggest anything and you would lose that.<br/> <br/>Overall: Interesting. Nicely done.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Straight out of the camera eh? Nicely done. Very interesting combination of subjects - I like how there is a linking theme of ''lines''. I find the orange luminance highly intriguing. Critical stuff: Not much really, hard to argue with a zero edit - suggest anything and you would lose that. Overall: Interesting. Nicely done.', '2010-02-07 15:04:55.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(5856923, 844884, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is pretty special - I like it a lot.</td>', 'This is pretty special - I like it a lot.', '2010-02-07 15:06:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856924, 851078, 100393, '<td valign="top">Masterfully done - I predict the front page for this one.</td>', 'Masterfully done - I predict the front page for this one.', '2010-02-07 15:07:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856927, 850012, 71872, '<td valign="top">Excellent shot. Perfect potrail of "All that is British" somehow finding a pleasurable insight into the bain of our lives.</td>', 'Excellent shot. Perfect potrail of "All that is British" somehow finding a pleasurable insight into the bain of our lives.', '2010-02-07 15:08:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856932, 851027, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is just great, the long exposure clouds - the output from the chimneys (they look they are blasting vapour out), the stark scenery, the grain/noise and the light all conspire to offer something that is more than the sum of its parts.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Just the little round aberration towards the left hand side, about 3/4 of the way up - dust spot? <br/> <br/>Overall: Very nice image, nicely shot - well thought through at the point of capture.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is just great, the long exposure clouds - the output from the chimneys (they look they are blasting vapour out), the stark scenery, the grain/noise and the light all conspire to offer something that is more than the sum of its parts. Critical stuff: Just the little round aberration towards the left hand side, about 3/4 of the way up - dust spot?  Overall: Very nice image, nicely shot - well thought through at the point of capture.', '2010-02-07 15:11:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856933, 850540, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wow - two phase exposure with zoom and use of lens cap?<br/> <br/>Nicely done.</td>', 'Wow - two phase exposure with zoom and use of lens cap? Nicely done.', '2010-02-07 15:12:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856939, 850950, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wow - so shadow-like, it took my brain a few seconds to work out that it wasn''t. Great coloration and interesting lighting.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I think the prominence of the central pillar means that you might have been better to have put that vertical. I''m not so keen on the red halo at the back of the rider - chromatic aberration?<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice, but for me, I think it just needs a bit of a neater edit.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wow - so shadow-like, it took my brain a few seconds to work out that it wasn''t. Great coloration and interesting lighting. Critical stuff: I think the prominence of the central pillar means that you might have been better to have put that vertical. I''m not so keen on the red halo at the back of the rider - chromatic aberration? Overall: Nice, but for me, I think it just needs a bit of a neater edit.', '2010-02-07 15:17:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856940, 851084, 100393, '<td valign="top">Very nicely composed.</td>', 'Very nicely composed.', '2010-02-07 15:17:47.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856945, 850612, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Nice and grungy - love the wall colour too; adds to the 50''s feel. I think you have offered just the right amount of texture here too. I like the clean composition with the true verticals and horizontals.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really.<br/> <br/>Overall: Very nice image - makes me want to know more about the scene.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Nice and grungy - love the wall colour too; adds to the 50''s feel. I think you have offered just the right amount of texture here too. I like the clean composition with the true verticals and horizontals. Critical stuff: Nothing really. Overall: Very nice image - makes me want to know more about the scene.', '2010-02-07 15:20:58.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856947, 850955, 24486, '<td valign="top">There is so much energy in this photograph that you don''t know where to look first.</td>', 'There is so much energy in this photograph that you don''t know where to look first.', '2010-02-07 15:23:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856950, 851177, 24486, '<td valign="top">Great action shot!</td>', 'Great action shot!', '2010-02-07 15:23:24.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856951, 850800, 24486, '<td valign="top">I never get tired looking at photographs like this. Excellant work</td>', 'I never get tired looking at photographs like this. Excellant work', '2010-02-07 15:24:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856966, 846813, 61961, '<td valign="top">I appreciate this natural landscape and that you didn''t succumb to over-processing.</td>', 'I appreciate this natural landscape and that you didn''t succumb to over-processing.', '2010-02-07 15:43:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856971, 850212, 64086, '<td valign="top">Amazing Shot. I love the light on the beach.</td>', 'Amazing Shot. I love the light on the beach.', '2010-02-07 15:51:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856972, 851178, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: The highlight for me in this image is the shadow of the dog - I like how squared off it is. I also like the texture of the iron work.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Most of everything else (sorry!) The off vertical structure really bothers me - my problem I know - I tend to be fussy about alignment (always better to align verticals than horizontals I think). The harshness of the contrast  -the very bright highlights in the bottom right corner seem unnecessarily harsh to me. The overall composition seems messy too.<br/> <br/>Overall: I''ve been trying to see what you have seen here, but I''m afraid I''ve failed.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: The highlight for me in this image is the shadow of the dog - I like how squared off it is. I also like the texture of the iron work. Critical stuff: Most of everything else (sorry!) The off vertical structure really bothers me - my problem I know - I tend to be fussy about alignment (always better to align verticals than horizontals I think). The harshness of the contrast  -the very bright highlights in the bottom right corner seem unnecessarily harsh to me. The overall composition seems messy too. Overall: I''ve been trying to see what you have seen here, but I''m afraid I''ve failed.', '2010-02-07 15:51:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856974, 851279, 100393, '<td valign="top">Great portrait the slight touch of colour in the eyes works really well.</td>', 'Great portrait the slight touch of colour in the eyes works really well.', '2010-02-07 15:52:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856976, 845917, 64086, '<td valign="top">Wow! This is the best picture of a seagull I have ever seen. The clarity is fantastic. I love the reflection of the feet on the ice.</td>', 'Wow! This is the best picture of a seagull I have ever seen. The clarity is fantastic. I love the reflection of the feet on the ice.', '2010-02-07 15:54:44.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856977, 851212, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Wow - what a brave juxtaposition, even more so when emphasised with the selective desaturation. It is very well executed though - great lighting, great textures, nice DOF.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing to suggest on the editing front - I might have been tempted to shoot it with a lower POV, but that''s just me.<br/> <br/>Overall: Interesting; would love to know more about your motivation for the picture.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Wow - what a brave juxtaposition, even more so when emphasised with the selective desaturation. It is very well executed though - great lighting, great textures, nice DOF. Critical stuff: Nothing to suggest on the editing front - I might have been tempted to shoot it with a lower POV, but that''s just me. Overall: Interesting; would love to know more about your motivation for the picture.', '2010-02-07 15:55:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856981, 846775, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This works really well; I like the ''woody'' colour palette too, it suits the subject matter.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much, I think this could''ve stood a tighter crop.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice work.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This works really well; I like the ''woody'' colour palette too, it suits the subject matter. Critical stuff: Not much, I think this could''ve stood a tighter crop. Overall: Nice work.', '2010-02-07 15:58:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856985, 851200, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: You''ve really created something interesting in your capture of this scene. The fall of the light on the crystalline ice and the change in colour towards the bottom of that element is highly compelling.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much at all really.<br/> <br/>Overall: Nice image, good to see something so pretty from a simple sheet of glass.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: You''ve really created something interesting in your capture of this scene. The fall of the light on the crystalline ice and the change in colour towards the bottom of that element is highly compelling. Critical stuff: Not much at all really. Overall: Nice image, good to see something so pretty from a simple sheet of glass.', '2010-02-07 16:02:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856989, 851095, 68586, '<td valign="top">very nice shot</td>', 'very nice shot', '2010-02-07 16:04:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856992, 850703, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: Interesting piece of graffiti. Good use of texture.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: I''m not sure your photography has added anything here, in fact I feel we could make a case that it has reduced the scene - sometimes that can be good, where the photographer captures an essence and the image becomes a distillation. But here, I don''t form that impression.... I feel you may have thrown the baby out with the bath water.<br/> <br/>Overall: An interesting scene perhaps but I''m sorry I don''t find this to be an interesting capture of that scene.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: Interesting piece of graffiti. Good use of texture. Critical stuff: I''m not sure your photography has added anything here, in fact I feel we could make a case that it has reduced the scene - sometimes that can be good, where the photographer captures an essence and the image becomes a distillation. But here, I don''t form that impression.... I feel you may have thrown the baby out with the bath water. Overall: An interesting scene perhaps but I''m sorry I don''t find this to be an interesting capture of that scene.', '2010-02-07 16:06:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856993, 850940, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: This is really nice and very well seen, we can see enough of their faces in the reflection to make this very interesting. I think the furniture contributes to the interest too.<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Not much really - perhaps a little more contrast, though perhaps that would obliterate the faces.<br/> <br/>Overall: A great scene, well captured.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: This is really nice and very well seen, we can see enough of their faces in the reflection to make this very interesting. I think the furniture contributes to the interest too. Critical stuff: Not much really - perhaps a little more contrast, though perhaps that would obliterate the faces. Overall: A great scene, well captured.', '2010-02-07 16:13:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(5856994, 847751, 100393, '<td valign="top">Oh, this is really wonderful - I''ve done a few aquarium shots, but none as good as this one. Perfect silhouettes. The smaller child particularly.</td>', 'Oh, this is really wonderful - I''ve done a few aquarium shots, but none as good as this one. Perfect silhouettes. The smaller child particularly.', '2010-02-07 16:15:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(5857000, 851052, 100393, '<td valign="top">Wow - this is pretty spectacular, it could be a poster or a Christmas card.</td>', 'Wow - this is pretty spectacular, it could be a poster or a Christmas card.', '2010-02-07 16:18:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(5857035, 851290, 100393, '<td valign="top">I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images. <br/> <br/>Positives: I like the way the context of this rather bizarre image is left so open - the suit, the white tiles make this a very open image. It can be interpreted through both humorous and sinister lenses. I particularly like the manic eyes - a touch of the Ray Liotta''s about them<br/> <br/>Critical stuff: Nothing really.<br/> <br/>Overall: A most interesting offering - I am really glad to have seen it.</td>', 'I''m going through the entries, stopping at those images I feel have had the benefit of an unconventional eye and dwelling a little longer to try to see and appreciate what you saw. This is one of those images.  Positives: I like the way the context of this rather bizarre image is left so open - the suit, the white tiles make this a very open image. It can be interpreted through both humorous and sinister lenses. I particularly like the manic eyes - a touch of the Ray Liotta''s about them Critical stuff: Nothing really. Overall: A most interesting offering - I am really glad to have seen it.', '2010-02-07 16:49:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(5857054, 851011, 68546, '<td valign="top">fantastic! Love this shot. well done</td>', 'fantastic! Love this shot. well done', '2010-02-07 17:08:14.000000', NULL, 1),
