(5859872, 848891, 30982, '<td valign="top">Woefully underrated.  I suspect it may be in part those who simply don''t like tattoos because the photography is really quite good here.  Nice work with the strobist setup and very good fine-tuning in your processing.  I suspect Jon really rather likes it, yes?  That''s way better than a score here.</td>', 'Woefully underrated.  I suspect it may be in part those who simply don''t like tattoos because the photography is really quite good here.  Nice work with the strobist setup and very good fine-tuning in your processing.  I suspect Jon really rather likes it, yes?  That''s way better than a score here.', '2010-02-08 21:46:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(5859900, 848891, 96793, '<td valign="top">Thanks so much Melethia. its really encouraging to hear support from talented photographers like Love and yourself. i was hoping to do a little better ( break 6 possibly) but i like how the photo came out and im glad to hear that other people like it too :)<br/> <br/>ps: jon loved them. i have several more in my portfolio on here. even ones without his hat.<br/> <br/>-Max</td>', 'Thanks so much Melethia. its really encouraging to hear support from talented photographers like Love and yourself. i was hoping to do a little better ( break 6 possibly) but i like how the photo came out and im glad to hear that other people like it too :) ps: jon loved them. i have several more in my portfolio on here. even ones without his hat. -Max', '2010-02-08 21:59:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(5859910, 847403, 18799, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club...<br/> <br/>This is going to be easy to critique as I don''t see anything I would do differently.  It''s a gorgeous image!  Excellent use of the foreground element to pull the eye into the image.<br/> <br/>I guess the only question I would have would be why the vertical landscape?  Maybe the lens wasn''t wide enough to get both the foreground element and the mountain tops in frame? Of course the composition is a personal thing, I just find myself wanting to see more of of the landscape.<br/> <br/>Well done, congrats.</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club... This is going to be easy to critique as I don''t see anything I would do differently.  It''s a gorgeous image!  Excellent use of the foreground element to pull the eye into the image. I guess the only question I would have would be why the vertical landscape?  Maybe the lens wasn''t wide enough to get both the foreground element and the mountain tops in frame? Of course the composition is a personal thing, I just find myself wanting to see more of of the landscape. Well done, congrats.', '2010-02-08 22:17:59.000000', NULL, 0),
