(5861331, 851110, 21432, '<td valign="top">Windsor Place.  The largest plantation ever built in Mississippi in the 1890''s.  It didn''t last long, it burned down about six years after it was completed.  It was used as a backdrop for the Movie "Rain Tree County" with Elizabeth Taylor and Montgomery Cliff shot in the early fifties.  Nice color and angle, good shot.  Hopefully you also had the time to visit the Church while you were there.  Both of these are way off the beaten path.</td>', 'Windsor Place.  The largest plantation ever built in Mississippi in the 1890''s.  It didn''t last long, it burned down about six years after it was completed.  It was used as a backdrop for the Movie "Rain Tree County" with Elizabeth Taylor and Montgomery Cliff shot in the early fifties.  Nice color and angle, good shot.  Hopefully you also had the time to visit the Church while you were there.  Both of these are way off the beaten path.', '2010-02-10 03:25:38.000000', NULL, 0),
